
# max-id: 1633
# test-passed: 409
# total-test: 412

id: 1000
level: 1
title: "BOMBrowser tests list"
--
id: 1001
level: 2
chapter_number: "1"
title: "Index"
text: "@@show_index(3,1)"
--
id: 1002
chapter_number: "2"
title: "Preface"
text:
    This document lists the technical requirements and the tests relatet to the project BOMBrowser.
    
--
id: 1003
chapter_number: "3"
title: "Requirements list"
text: "This chapter lists all the requirements."
--
id: 1008
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.1"
title: "Generic requirements"
text: "These chapters list all the requirements not specific to a single subsystem."
--
id: 1009
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.1.1"
title: "Common commands"
req:
    All windows shall support standard commands:
    - Help -> About
    - Window menu -> Close all other windows
    - Window menu -> Open a new 'Code list' window
    - Window menu -> List all open windows
    - File -> Close
    - File -> Quit
--
id: 1010
chapter_number: "3.1.2"
title: "Copy table"
req: "It shall be possible to copy a table displayed in a window."
--
id: 1464
chapter_number: "3.1.3"
title: "Document attached to a code"
req: "It shall be possible to link a drawing/document to a code."
--
id: 1465
chapter_number: "3.1.4"
title: "URL attached to a code"
req: "It shall be possible to link a URL to a code."
--
id: 1495
chapter_number: "3.1.5"
title: "URL attached to a code"
req: "It shall be possible to link a URL to a code."
--
id: 1513
chapter_number: "3.1.6"
title: "GVal properties"
req: "It shall be possible to attach custom properties to a code."
--
id: 1514
chapter_number: "3.1.7"
title: "GAVal properties"
req: "It shall be possible to attach custom properties to a child item of an assembly."
--
id: 1616
chapter_number: "3.1.8"
title: "Check db connection"
req: "BOMBrowser shall check the db connection and try to reconnect in few attempts."
--
id: 1632
chapter_number: "3.1.9"
title: "Self test"
req: "BOMBrowser shall have some self test to run during the verification fase"
--
id: 1004
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.2"
title: "'Code list window' requirements"
text: "These chapters list all the requirements related to the assembly window."
--
id: 1005
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.2.1"
title: "Search fields - code and description"
req: "The 'Code list window' shall allow searching for codes by 'code' and 'description'."
--
id: 1006
chapter_number: "3.2.2"
title: "Search fields - wildcards"
req: 'Search can be performed using wildcard characters such as "_" and "%" according to the standard SQL syntax, as well as operators like >, <, =, !.'
--
id: 1460
chapter_number: "3.2.3"
title: "Code property"
req: "On the right side of the window, a panel shall display all properties of the highlighted code."
--
id: 1461
chapter_number: "3.2.4"
title: "Status bar"
req:
    At the bottom of the window, a status bar shall display:
    - the query execution time
    - the number of results
--
id: 1462
chapter_number: "3.2.5"
title: "Revision search"
req: "The 'Code GUI window' shall allow searching for revisions across all available fields."
--
id: 1463
chapter_number: "3.2.6"
title: "Revision search result colors"
req: "In the 'Search revision window', it shall be possible to apply custom row colors."
--
id: 1007
chapter_number: "3.2.7"
title: "Code commands"
req:
    From the result area, it shall be possible to trigger the following commands:
    - Show assembly
    - Where used
    - Copy / Revise code
    - Edit code
    - Diff command
--
id: 1470
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.3"
title: "'Code GUI' panel requirements"
text: "These chapters list all the requirements related to the 'Code GUI' panel."
--
id: 1471
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.3.1"
title: "The 'Code GUI' panel shows code properties"
req:
    The 'Code GUI' panel shall display code/revision properties such as:
     - Code
     - Description
     - Revision
     - Iteration
     - Date from
     - Date to
     - Documents
     - gvalX variables
source-requirements: [1513]
--
id: 1466
chapter_number: "3.3.2"
title: "The 'Code GUI' revisions list box"
req:
    The 'Code GUI' panel shall include a list box displaying different revision
    dates. Selecting a revision/date updates the 'Code GUI' panel with the corresponding properties.
--
id: 1467
chapter_number: "3.3.3"
title: "The 'Code GUI' copy button"
req: "The 'Code GUI' panel shall feature a copy button that copies all properties to the clipboard."
--
id: 1468
chapter_number: "3.3.4"
title: "The 'Code GUI' 'Document' button"
req:
    The 'Code GUI' panel shall display a button for each document.
    Hovering over a button displays a tooltip showing the document properties.
    Clicking the button opens the document or URL.
    Right-clicking (RMB) the button opens a context menu with the following commands:
    - Copy filename: copies the filename to the clipboard
    - Copy dirname: copies the directory path of the file to the clipboard
    - Copy fullname: copies the full path (directory + filename) to the clipboard
    - Copy file: copies the file object to the clipboard
    - Open dir: opens the directory containing the file
    - Copy description: copies the description to the clipboard
    - Copy URL: copies the URL to the clipboard
--
id: 1469
chapter_number: "3.3.5"
title: "The 'Code GUI' 'Document' button text length"
req: "It shall be possible to configure the maximum filename length displayed on the button caption."
--
id: 1480
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.4"
title: "Assembly/Where used window requirements"
text: "This chapter lists all requirements related to the Assembly / Where Used window."
--
id: 1485
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.4.1"
title: "Content of the assembly window"
req:
    The 'Assembly window' can display the following hierarchical structures:
    - Assembly BOM (latest - i.e., showing only codes with an open 'Date to')
    - Assembly BOM for a specific date
    - Prototype assembly BOM
    - Where used
    - Valid where used (i.e., showing only codes with an open 'Date to')
    - Smart where used (similar to the above, but displaying only the first 2 levels and the top-level code)
--
id: 1490
chapter_number: "3.4.2"
title: "Code GUI panel"
req: "In the Assembly / Where Used window, a 'Code GUI' panel shall be present on the right side."
--
id: 1481
chapter_number: "3.4.3"
title: "Select date"
req: "For the 'Show assembly by date' command, a dialog shall allow selecting a specific BOM date to display."
--
id: 1482
chapter_number: "3.4.4"
title: "Export to JSON"
req: "It shall be possible to export the displayed data in JSON format."
--
id: 1483
chapter_number: "3.4.5"
title: "Show/hide levels"
req: "It shall be possible to show or hide different levels of the BOM."
--
id: 1486
chapter_number: "3.4.6"
title: "Search in BOM"
req: "It shall be possible to search by code and description within the BOM."
--
id: 1487
chapter_number: "3.4.7"
title: "Loop detection"
req: "The system shall detect circular references (loops) in the hierarchical structure."
--
id: 1488
chapter_number: "3.4.8"
title: "Export"
req: "It shall be possible to export the data displayed in the window."
--
id: 1489
chapter_number: "3.4.9"
title: "BOM Coloring"
req: "It shall be possible to color-code the displayed data based on property values."
--
id: 1502
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.5"
title: "Diff window requirements"
--
id: 1493
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.5.1"
title: "Diff window main requirements"
req:
    It shall be possible to compare two BOMs based on:
    - part lists of each assembly
    - properties (description, revisions, documents, etc.) of each code
    - added codes, removed codes, and updated codes
    The BOMs shall be selected by code and date.
--
id: 1494
chapter_number: "3.5.2"
title: "Diff window options"
req: "The Diff window shall provide an option to swap the two BOMs, inverting the '+' (added) and '-' (removed) markers."
--
id: 1503
chapter_number: "3.5.3"
title: "Diff window options (2)"
req: "The Diff window shall provide an option to display only key attributes (code, description, revision)."
--
id: 1504
chapter_number: "3.5.4"
title: "Diff window options (3)"
req: "The Diff window shall provide an option to compare only the first level of child items."
--
id: 1505
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.6"
title: "Edit functions"
--
id: 1506
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.6.1"
title: "Copy code"
req: "It shall be possible to copy a code."
--
id: 1507
chapter_number: "3.6.2"
title: "Revise the code"
req:
    It shall be possible to revise a code.
    The code identifier remains identical, but all other attributes may change.
    The date must be different and cannot be earlier than the date of the latest revision.
    It shall be possible to create a prototype revision.
--
id: 1509
chapter_number: "3.6.3"
title: "Edit code: edit code properties"
req: "It shall be possible to modify the properties of a code revision (description, revision, etc.)."
--
id: 1510
chapter_number: "3.6.4"
title: "Edit code: edit child items"
req:
    It shall be possible to modify the child items of a code:
    - add a child code
    - remove a child code
    - modify the quantity of a child code
    - reorder child items
    - copy a child item from one code to another
    - search for a code to insert
--
id: 1511
chapter_number: "3.6.5"
title: "Edit code: edit code drawings"
req:
    It shall be possible to manage drawings attached to a code:
    - add a drawing
    - remove a drawing
    - add a URL
    - remove a URL
    It shall be possible to display a drawing directly from the edit window.
source-requirements: [1464, 1495]
--
id: 1515
chapter_number: "3.6.6"
title: "Edit code: edit code drawings - copy and paste drawings"
req: "It shall be possible to copy drawings from one code to another."
--
id: 1512
chapter_number: "3.6.7"
title: "Edit code: remove a revision"
req: "It shall be possible to delete a code or a specific code revision."
--
id: 1518
chapter_number: "3.6.8"
title: "Edit code: change revision date"
req: "It shall be possible to update the date of a revision."
--
id: 1520
chapter_number: "3.6.9"
title: "Edit code: change revision date validation"
req:
    During a date update, the following validation checks must be performed:
    - the dates must be valid calendar dates
    - the dates must be consecutive
    - date ranges between revisions must not overlap
    - if a date is updated, every child item must outlive its parent
    - it shall be possible to set only the latest revision's 'Date to' as prototype
    - it shall be possible to set the latest revision's 'Date to' as prototype, empty (infinity), or a finite date
    - each 'Date to' must be greater than or equal to 'Date from'
--
id: 1609
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.7"
title: "Config file requirements"
--
id: 1610
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.7.1"
title: "Config file: basic requirements"
req:
    - BOMBrowser must be configured by a config file named 'bombrowser.ini',
      stored in the same directory as the executable.
    - Alternatively, a file named 'bombrowser.forward' (containing the absolute
      path of the 'bombrowser.ini' file) can be used to specify the path to
      the config file.
--
id: 1612
chapter_number: "3.7.2"
title: "Config file: force upper case"
req:
    BOMBrowser can be configured to force all codes and/or descriptions
    to uppercase.
--
id: 1613
chapter_number: "3.7.3"
title: "Config file: search ignore case"
req: "BOMBrowser can be configured so that searches are case-insensitive."
--
id: 1614
chapter_number: "3.7.4"
title: "Config file: check file"
req:
    During startup, BOMBrowser shall perform basic integrity checks on the
    'bombrowser.ini' file.
--
id: 1615
chapter_number: "3.7.5"
title: "Config file: default search mode"
req:
    BOMBrowser can be configured so that it starts the "Code list" window in
    standard or advance search mode.
--
id: 1617
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.8"
title: "Advanced search in BOM"
--
id: 1618
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.8.1"
title: "Search in BOM"
req:
    BOMBrowser shall allow to search a code of a BOM in the assembly window.
    This search, called "Advance search", can be executed on any property of
    a code like: code, description, unit, gval...
    It can be possible to use operator like >, <, !
--
id: 1619
chapter_number: "3.8.2"
title: "Search document in BOM"
req:
    BOMBrowser shall allow to search a code of a BOM in the assembly window.
    This search, called "Advance search", can be executed on document.
--
id: 1620
chapter_number: "3.8.3"
title: "Search in '[smart/valid] where used windows'"
req:
    BOMBrowser shall allow to search a code of '[smart/valid] where used windows'.
    This search, called "Advance search", can be executed on any property of
    a code like: code, description, unit, gval....
--
id: 1621
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.9"
title: "Export data from BOM"
--
id: 1622
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.9.1"
title: "Export data, main requirements"
req:
    BOMBrowser shall allow to export all the iformation of a BOM:
    - the BOM in a CSV file
    - all the file contained in the BOM
--
id: 1623
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.10"
title: "Database management"
--
id: 1624
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.10.1"
title: "Dump database"
req: "BOMBrowser shall allow to dump the database"
--
id: 1625
chapter_number: "3.10.2"
title: "Restore database"
req: "BOMBrowser shall allow to restore a database from a dump"
--
id: 1626
chapter_number: "3.10.3"
title: "Create a new database"
req:
    BOMBrowser shall allow to create a new database. Only the code 000000000000
    shall exist.
--
id: 1627
chapter_number: "3.10.4"
title: "Create a new database"
req: "The database restore shall consider the count of gval/agval variables."
--
id: 1628
level: 3
chapter_number: "3.11"
title: "Log transaction"
--
id: 1629
level: 4
chapter_number: "3.11.1"
title: "Log transaction: actions to log"
req:
    BOMBrowser shall log all the database changes:
    - create a new revision
    - copy a code
    - edit a code
    - remove/add a document
    - remove/add a child
    - change a date
    - delete a revision
    - delete a code
--
id: 1630
chapter_number: "3.11.2"
title: "Log transaction: cannot write the log"
req: "BOMBrowser shall inform that it is not possible to log the action."
--
id: 1631
chapter_number: "3.11.3"
title: "Log transaction: compress the log"
req: "BOMBrowser shall allow to compress the log in .gz format."
--
id: 1011
level: 2
chapter_number: "4"
title: "Tests list"
text:
    Before executing the tests, verify that the following bombrowser.init parameters are set as shown:
    
    BOMBROWSER.description_force_uppercase=1
    BOMBROWSER.code_force_uppercase=1
    BOMBROWSER.ignore_case_during_search=1
    BOMBROWSER.db=sqlite
    
    SQLITE.ignore_case_during_search=0
    
    Set up the DB with:
    
    python mkdb.py --test_db
--
